        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: align iOS icons with favicon mark",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe iOS and Watch icon catalogs still used an older lobster silhouette while the OpenClaw UI and web favicon use the newer rounded mascot. The original asset refresh also made all 42 Debug/production icon pairs byte-identical, removing the visual safety cue that distinguishes development installs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nProduction iOS and Watch icons now use the canonical favicon mark. Debug icons keep the same mark inside a white inset panel with full-bleed yellow/navy construction stripes and a navy bug badge. The Watch in-app fallback remains a transparent favicon-derived raster for circular UI rendering.\n\n## User Impact\n\nApple launch, store, companion, and fallback surfaces now match the current OpenClaw identity. Developers can still distinguish Debug builds immediately at every supported iOS and Watch icon size.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `da200a6c68025140bbecddae40e158cbcdd9ad2e`.\n- Verified all 42 Debug/production pairs differ and retain identical dimensions.\n- Verified all 84 app-icon PNGs are opaque and all four asset-catalog manifests reference existing files.\n- Generated and visually inspected a 2200×1720 contact sheet covering iOS and Watch production/debug icons at marketing, home-screen, and small sizes; SHA-256 `a94c3f0d50bd8fa715eec55d796a3622783b4b4a71d760049992622eab6c0359`.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Fresh autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Exact-head CI run [`29006727667`](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29006727667): all required checks passed, including `macos-swift`, `ios-build`, and `native-i18n`.\n\nThe approved artifact publisher was unavailable, so the contact sheet is retained with the maintainer proof rather than committed to the product repository.\n",
